{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 1362070,
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "25890082",
      "title": "Summary & Further Resources",
      "sourceHash": "c4e1ea4d571aa9a39d862b51ab982435c314f8b4be57632a613b67c48a3c6c5a",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.21,
          "end": 3.99,
          "en": "Now that's it for this module,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.99,
          "end": 6.88,
          "en": "which is only an introduction to testing",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 6.88,
          "end": 9.25,
          "en": "or to testing React apps.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 9.25,
          "end": 11.7,
          "en": "Now, testing as I mentioned at the beginning",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 11.7,
          "end": 15.91,
          "en": "is definitely a topic an entire course could be created on.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 15.91,
          "end": 18.54,
          "en": "But this course is not about that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 18.54,
          "end": 20.68,
          "en": "It's about React and therefore I want",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 20.68,
          "end": 23.15,
          "en": "to introduce you to React testing.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 23.15,
          "end": 26.02,
          "en": "I don't want to include an entire testing course",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 26.02,
          "end": 27.803,
          "en": "into this course as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 28.78,
          "end": 30.61,
          "en": "Now, if you want to learn more about testing,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 30.61,
          "end": 33.36,
          "en": "of course there are dedicated tutorials and courses",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 33.36,
          "end": 34.52,
          "en": "you can check out.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 34.52,
          "end": 36.837,
          "en": "But what's also definitely worth a look,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 36.837,
          "end": 39.443,
          "en": "are the official docs of Jest.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 39.443,
          "end": 41.04,
          "en": "This tool we used under the hood",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 41.04,
          "end": 44.13,
          "en": "for running our tests and for asserting the results",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 44.13,
          "end": 47.133,
          "en": "and the docs of the React testing library.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 48.17,
          "end": 49.5,
          "en": "Now let's start with Jest.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 49.5,
          "end": 52,
          "en": "If you Google for Jest you find these official docs",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 52,
          "end": 54.9,
          "en": "and these docs aren't too bad.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 54.9,
          "end": 57.66,
          "en": "Now, keep in mind that all these setup steps here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 57.66,
          "end": 60.91,
          "en": "are not required by you because in our React project",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 60.91,
          "end": 62.61,
          "en": "you already have a setup.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 62.61,
          "end": 64.34,
          "en": "And also keep in mind here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 64.34,
          "end": 69.12,
          "en": "that Jest is not a tool focused on just React.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 69.12,
          "end": 72.44,
          "en": "It's a general JavaScript testing tool,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 72.44,
          "end": 75.35,
          "en": "and therefore the docs represent that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 75.35,
          "end": 76.97,
          "en": "But still here, you can learn more",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 76.97,
          "end": 79.36,
          "en": "about the different matchers, which you have,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 79.36,
          "end": 82.72,
          "en": "the different ways of expressing expectations.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 82.72,
          "end": 85.9,
          "en": "You can learn more about testing async code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 85.9,
          "end": 90.27,
          "en": "How you can wait for promises to complete, if you want that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 90.27,
          "end": 92.66,
          "en": "You can learn more about mocking functions,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 92.66,
          "end": 95.3,
          "en": "something we also did in this module.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 95.3,
          "end": 97.46000000000001,
          "en": "Here you can dive deeper and learn more",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 97.46000000000001,
          "end": 99.89,
          "en": "about the possibilities you've got there,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 99.89,
          "end": 102.13,
          "en": "for mocking regular functions.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 102.13,
          "end": 105.61,
          "en": "And also of course, for mocking promises,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 105.61,
          "end": 108.16,
          "en": "as we did it here as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 108.16,
          "end": 110.47999999999999,
          "en": "You can learn more here and in general.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 110.47999999999999,
          "end": 112.92,
          "en": "Check out these different guides here to learn",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 112.92,
          "end": 115.88,
          "en": "about the different examples and the different features",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 115.88,
          "end": 117.65299999999999,
          "en": "this tool has to offer.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 118.88,
          "end": 121.19,
          "en": "Now, when it comes to testing React",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 121.19,
          "end": 124.74,
          "en": "you want to check out the React Testing Library docs.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 124.74,
          "end": 128.57,
          "en": "These docs are also great, and in there you learn way more",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 128.57,
          "end": 131.71,
          "en": "about testing React with that library.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 131.71,
          "end": 134.9,
          "en": "You also find a complete example here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 134.9,
          "end": 137.15,
          "en": "which could be interesting to check out.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 137.15,
          "end": 141.11,
          "en": "You find the complete API, which you have available.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 141.11,
          "end": 143.47,
          "en": "Also check out the core API here to learn",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 143.47,
          "end": 145.28,
          "en": "about these different query methods.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 145.28,
          "end": 148.32,
          "en": "GetBy, findBy, queryBy.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 148.32,
          "end": 151.69,
          "en": "You also get the differences explained here again.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 151.69,
          "end": 154.54,
          "en": "You also learn more about firing user events here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 154.54,
          "end": 156.77,
          "en": "You'll learn more about async code here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 156.77,
          "end": 160.79,
          "en": "and therefore that definitely also is a documentation",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 160.79,
          "end": 163.57,
          "en": "that is worth a closer look if you are serious",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 163.57,
          "end": 166.29,
          "en": "about testing React apps.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 166.29,
          "end": 171.19,
          "en": "I especially also want to highlight the ecosystem part here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 171.19,
          "end": 174.85,
          "en": "Where you learn about extensions, that you can install.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 174.85,
          "end": 177.24,
          "en": "Some of these extensions already are part",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 177.24,
          "end": 180.84,
          "en": "of a default project set up in a React app.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 180.84,
          "end": 185.72,
          "en": "For example, the user-event extension.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 185.72,
          "end": 188.16,
          "en": "But I especially also want to highlight one extension,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 188.16,
          "end": 189.83,
          "en": "which is not listed here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 189.83,
          "end": 193.7,
          "en": "And that is the React-hooks-testing-library extension,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 193.7,
          "end": 197.85,
          "en": "which makes testing React hooks especially custom hooks,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 197.85,
          "end": 199.073,
          "en": "way easier.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 199.97,
          "end": 202.24,
          "en": "Here you can learn how to use that extension",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 202.24,
          "end": 204.01,
          "en": "in case you have custom book functions,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 204.01,
          "end": 205.35,
          "en": "which you want to test.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 205.35,
          "end": 208.21,
          "en": "Which of course, typically do want to test",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 208.21,
          "end": 211.86,
          "en": "because you should test your entire code base if possible.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 211.86,
          "end": 215.05,
          "en": "And therefore these are resources you can dive",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 215.05,
          "end": 217.36,
          "en": "in as a next step, but I hope",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 217.36,
          "end": 220.88,
          "en": "that this course module gets you started with testing",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 220.88,
          "end": 223.41,
          "en": "and you now at least have a general idea",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 223.41,
          "end": 225.223,
          "en": "of how that all works.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}